{
    "background_story": "Ellis grew up with ice skates strapped to his feet, spending every spare moment at the local rink. He began as a shy, gangly kid, but as he glided across the frozen surface, he found his confidence and his calling. Ellis's dedication paid off as he rose through the ranks of junior hockey, eventually earning a scholarship to play for a top-tier university team. The rink became his sanctuary, a place where he could escape the pressures of everyday life and lose himself in the rush of competition. As he entered the professional leagues, Ellis became known for his lightning-fast reflexes and uncanny ability to read the game. Despite the grueling schedule and physical demands, he never lost his love for the rink, where he had found his true home and his sense of purpose.",
